  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "View all Brussels is world-renowned as the political heart of the European Union, featuring the European Parliament and Commission. It is famous for its culinary delights—specifically chocolate, waffles, beer, and fries—as well as the ornate Grand Place, the Atomium, and the Manneken Pis statue. Key highlights of what Brussels is known for include: Political Hub: Known as the \"Capital of Europe,\" hosting major EU institutions and NATO headquarters. Gastronomy: World-famous for Belgian waffles, premium chocolate (pralines), and a rich beer culture, featuring diverse styles. Historic Architecture: The Grand Place is a UNESCO World Heritage site known for its stunning 17th-century guild houses, Baroque architecture, and City Hall. Iconic Landmarks: The Atomium (a giant, stainless steel unit cell of an iron crystal) and the Manneken Pis (a small bronze statue of a peeing boy) are iconic attractions. Culture & Arts: A vibrant art scene featuring the Magritte Museum, comic strip murals, and Art Nouveau architecture. The city is also a bilingual hub (French and Dutch) with a rich history of lace-making and a central location for exploring Belgian culture.",
